318825310334647,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":61.9,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.016585460175163144,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":79.3,"_gate_piotroski":2,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":22.2,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.048383442093950846,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":59.4,"_gate_rev_durability":0.029843848195707734,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":39.9,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.06257703483296077,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.014502795512977507,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":31.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004282890401932792,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":92.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.00316,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Lincoln National Corporation, through its subsidiaries, operates multiple insurance and retirement businesses in the United States. It operates through four segments: Life Insurance, Annuities, Group Protection, and Retirement Plan Services. The Life Insurance segment provides life insurance products, including term insurance, universal life insurance (UL), indexed universal life insurance, variable universal life insurance (VUL), linked-benefit UL and VUL products, and critical illness and long-term care riders. Its Annuities segment offers variable, fixed, and registered index-linked annuities. The Group Protection segment offers group nonmedical insurance products consisting of short and long-term disability and administration services, statutory disability; paid family medical leave administration and absence management services; term life; life; supplemental health insurance; accident, critical illness, and hospital indemnity benefits and dental and vision products to the employer marketplace through various forms of employee-paid and employer-paid plans. Its Retirement Plan Services segment provides employers with retirement plan products and services primarily in the defined contribution retirement plan marketplace; individual and group variable annuities, group fixed annuities, and mutual fund-based programs; and various plan services, including plan recordkeeping, compliance testing, participant education, and trust and custodial services. It distributes its products through consultants, brokers, planners, agents, financial advisors, third-party administrators, financial institutions, and other intermediaries. Lincoln National Corporation was founded in 1905 and is headquartered in Radnor, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Ellen R. Gail Cooper C.F.A., F.S.A. | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 61 | Compensation: $7.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $1.9M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Lincoln National Corporation is a mid-cap financial services business with a $8.0B market cap on $18.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 6.9\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 6.3% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 20% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["41 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Lincoln National Corporation $LNC Stake Increased by Jefferies Financial Group Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/lincoln-national-corporation-lnc-stake-increased-by-jefferies-financial-group-inc.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794565634.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.866,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Lincoln National (LNC), What Is Behind The Fresh Attention Now?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nyse-lnc/lincoln-national/news/lincoln-national-lnc-what-is-behind-the-fresh-attention-now","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794511735.784,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.565,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Lincoln National Corporation (NYSE:LNC) Shareholders to Receive $0.45 Quarterly Dividend","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/lincoln-national-corporation-nyselnc-shareholders-to-receive-0-45-quarterly-dividend.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794415370.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Is Lincoln National (NYSE:LNC) Resuming Share Reductions?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/value/is-lincoln-national-nyselnc-resuming-share-reductions","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794385860.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Lincoln National (LNC) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/what-lincoln-n